 ### Step 3: Create Initial Playbooks (Based on Recent Issues)\
\
 Create 5 high-value playbooks from recent debugging sessions:\
\
 #### 3a. `playbooks/pod-debugging/image-pull-failures.md`\
 **Content from today's chat debugging**:\
 - Symptoms: ImagePullBackOff, ErrImagePull\
 - Investigation: Check registry connectivity, Kaniko build status\
 - Root causes: Registry timeout, missing image, TLS handshake failure\
 - Solutions: Verify build job, check registry service, test node connectivity\
 - Real example: Commit a6b1a31 (chat backend image issue)\
\
 #### 3b. `playbooks/network/metallb-l2-vpn-issues.md`\
 **Content from today's MetalLB debugging**:\
 - Symptoms: LoadBalancer IP not reachable over VPN\
 - Investigation: Ping test, check MetalLB speakers, verify L2Advertisement\
 - Root cause: L2 ARP doesn't cross routed VPN (Layer 3)\
 - Solution: Switch to NodePort for VPN access\
 - Real example: Commit c07013e (NodePort migration)\
\
 #### 3c. `playbooks/resources/limitrange-violations.md`\
 **Content from Qdrant deployment**:\
 - Symptoms: "forbidden: memory/cpu max limit to request ratio per Container"\
 - Investigation: Check namespace LimitRange, compare pod resource specs\
 - Root cause: Resource request:limit ratio exceeds policy (4:1 CPU, 2:1 memory)\
 - Solution: Adjust resource requests to comply with ratios\
 - Real example: Qdrant deployment fix (from session summary)\
\
 #### 3d. `playbooks/gitops/argocd-sync-failures.md`\
 **Content from today's ArgoCD issues**:\
 - Symptoms: Application status "Unknown", sync errors, "ComparisonError"\
 - Investigation: Check application status, review sync logs, verify repo connectivity\
 - Root causes: Redis timeout, repo auth failure, manifest parsing errors\
 - Solutions: Manual kubectl apply, force refresh, fix YAML syntax\
 - Real example: cortex-chat ArgoCD sync timeout\
\
 #### 3e. `playbooks/gitops/kaniko-build-timeouts.md`\
 **Content from MoE router builds**:\
 - Symptoms: "dial tcp 10.43.170.72:5000: i/o timeout"\
 - Investigation: Test registry connectivity, check build pod logs, verify network policies\
 - Root causes: Registry service down, network policy blocking, node network issues\
 - Solutions: Restart registry, verify service endpoints, check NetworkPolicy rules\
 - Real example: MoE router build attempts\
\
